  "interpretation": [
    "Compressed full-canvas checkpoints are materially broader than persistent tiles: at the 32 MiB/eight-frame reference point, 80 of 280 ratio cases are retained-state feasible and 42 also clear the modeled-peak hard cap.",
    "Peak-clearing cases exist only for encoded-source-retained 1024-square scenarios. FULL-1024-60 clears through a 25 percent checkpoint-blob ratio, SUBRECT-NONE-1024-60 through 50 percent, and SUBRECT-PREVIOUS-1024-120 through 10 percent under both access profiles.",
    "No 2048-square reference case clears the modeled-peak hard cap. With separate straight-alpha compositor and premultiplied output surfaces, the two canvases alone consume exactly 32 MiB.",
    "The 38 native checkpoint blobs round-trip exactly. Their observed ratios range from 0.1534 percent to 12.5725 percent with a 1.57 percent median, but these small-fixture ratios are not extrapolated to scaled production content or decode latency.",
    "Raw-subrect-retained strategies generally fail the reference point because total decoded track bytes dominate. The viable compressed envelope retains encoded source and decodes subrect payloads during replay.",
    "The next production decision is not simply another checkpoint representation: Fovea must either constrain supported canvas size, permit an output-buffer alias/destructive finalization mode, or revise what the 32 MiB hard cap covers. Dirty-region state alone cannot remove a two-canvas transient floor."
  ],
  "claimBoundary": {
    "formalClaimEligible": false,
    "reasons": [
      "Synthetic checkpoint blob ratios are explicit sensitivity inputs from 0.25 percent through 100 percent; they are not inferred from native fixture compression.",
      "The checkpoint blob stores the complete straight-alpha pre-frame canvas with a deterministic header, zlib payload, dimensions, raw byte count, and CRC32.",
      "Frame zero uses an implicit transparent pre-frame state and retains no compressed blob.",
      "Modeled peak counts retained source or raw subrect state, retained compressed checkpoints, one straight-alpha compositor canvas, the largest current raw subrect, the largest previous-disposal save region, one premultiplied output canvas, and 256 KiB decompressor workspace.",
      "The model excludes allocator fragmentation, ImageIO private state, compression latency, CPU, energy, thermal effects, and physical-device pressure.",
      "A feasible analytical ratio is a threshold requirement, not evidence that production animation content achieves that ratio or latency."
    ]
  },
